WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.030
NARRATOR: Nearly 6,000
feet up in the mountains,

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.940
another mom has
a huge challenge.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.930
A female black bear
has spent the winter

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.250
in a high mountain cave.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:25.800
She needs to teach her cubs
to survive in the park.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.530
With little to no food
or water for months,

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.060
the stakes are high.

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.960
But they're living
in a special place.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:38.450
Big Bend is the
only national park

00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:44.430
with an entire mountain range
inside its borders, the Chisos.

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:46.980
Named for their
previous inhabitants

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:51.570
and once home to the Mescalero
Apache and the Comanche tribes,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:55.880
the mountains are
a sky island oasis.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.410
40 square miles of
peaks up to 8,000 feet

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.390
loom over the hot desert below.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.920
At the height of
summer, monsoon storms

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.505
can dump nearly a year's
rainfall in a few months.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.880
Right now, the monsoon
is a long way off,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.410
but the Chisos do
something incredible.

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:33.470
They catch the rains and
store them for year round use.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:37.910
Water slowly releases
from deep in the mountains

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:48.990
into precious spring-fed
pools, attracting critters

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:55.240
of all types and all colors.

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:06.645
The key to survival in a desert
is a reliable source of water.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:16.590
And Mom knows exactly where
to find it thanks to her mom

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:22.010
who taught her about the
hidden oases in the Chisos.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:25.280
It's the cubs' first visit
to this magical place.

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.280
Every day is a school day.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.830
Today's lesson is
all about water.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:45.180
They've never tasted
or seen so much of it.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:59.480
Mom relaxes in the spring, but
for the cubs, it's play time.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.990
The fun has to come
to an end eventually,

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:31.000
but Mom has another lesson
for her eager students,

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:33.520
how to scratch that itch.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:43.090
Mom shows how it's done,
rubbing off her winter coat

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:47.170
and leaving a scent behind,
signaling her presence

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:49.120
to other bears in the park.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:59.290
Mom made it look
easy, but the cubs

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.685
will need a lot more practice.

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:14.800
For the bear family, the
Chisos mountains provide

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:17.500
water and a cool refuge.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:21.610
But down below on the desert
floor, life in the park

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:24.960
has more extreme challenges.

